  "title": "Chapter 3: Energy and Power",
  "order": 52,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qe05rt4",
      "content": "Energy and power are fundamental concepts in physics that explain the ability to do work and the rate at which work is done. Energy exists in many forms and can be converted from one form to another."
    },
