    {
      "id": "bm151qd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Law of Conservation of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1y8b1dl",
      "content": "The law of conservation of energy states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed; it can only be converted from one form to another."
    },
    {
      "id": "vug3f7z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Mechanical Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5bzx0lh",
      "content": "Mechanical energy is the sum of kinetic energy and potential energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ykde68k",
      "content": "Mechanical Energy = KE + PE"
    },
    {
      "id": "v1q9tse",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Meaning of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "let999g",
      "content": "Power is the rate at which work is done or energy is transferred."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xdqu5p3",
      "content": "Formula: Power = Work / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9hmztpv",
      "content": "SI Unit of Power = Watt (W)"
    },
    {
      "id": "xwdu57k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Units of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "If the velocity of an object is doubled, its Kinetic Energy becomes four times (4x) its original value.",
        "1 Horsepower (HP) is equal to 746 Watts, a frequently repeated numerical fact in SSC and Railway exams.",
        "Commercial unit of electricity is 1 kilowatt-hour (1 unit = 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules).",
        "When a body falls freely under gravity, its potential energy gradually converts into kinetic energy while total mechanical energy remains constant."
      ],
      "id": "7xddiyd"
    },
